      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-11-17_WidnesExaminer_art0023" n="art0023">
        <head>NEWS OF THE GNAE.</head>
        <p>NEWS OF THE GNAE.</p>
        <p>The annual meeting of the Lancashire Draughts Clubs' Association was held at 201, London-road, on Saturday last. The president, Mr. Frank Dunne, of Warrington, oe ipied t!,e chair. The minutes of the last annual mewing was read and confirmed, with a slight alteration. An abstract from the treasurer's balance-sheet was read, which showed that the association was well in funds. As the treasurer was unable to be present, the passing of the ricounts was po:tponed. 'The follow- ing len7leinen were then elected to hold office for the coming year :—President, Mr Joseph Townsend, Littl-borough ; vice-president, Mr. liichard Johnson, Liverpool; treasurer, Mr. J B.Holt, Rochdale-road, Bury ; secretary, Mr. John Ilynd, jun , 115, Fit zwarren-street, Pendleton, Man- chester. A discussion took place as to inviting Yorkshire to play a county match this seasonbut it appeared that no suitable holiday time was avail- able, as other fixturts had been arranged. It was decided not to play a tournament for the champion- ship of the county this year. The matches for the Love trophy" durinv. the corning season will be held on the" home and away" principle A vote of thanks was passd to the retiring officers . " Liverpool Mercury." The liettilquarters of the vVarrington Draughts' Club will in future be at Morris's Restaurant, Bank Quay, i;nd as there are many rising players in and around via,. neighbourhood, no doubt the club has a very bright prospect before it.</p>
