      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-11-17_WidnesExaminer_art0027" n="art0027">
        <head>EXAIVIINER FRIDAY NOVEMBER 17, 1899.</head>
        <p>THE EXAIVIINER FRIDAY NOVEMBER 17, 1899.</p>
        <p>THE MAYOR'S CHAPLAIN.</p>
        <p>The MAYOR appointed the Rev. John Wings, as his chaplain. His sai I that appointment brought him to an- other important matter. fie desired to attend the service at Wycliffe Congregational Church on Sunday morning next officially and he invited the whole of the members of the Council, the member, of the Board of Guardi alas, the general public and officials to accompany him. (Hear, hear.) Ho also wished to announce that it was his intention to visit the Parish Church in a similar way in the evenine. of Sunday next and he invited all the gentlemrn he had mentioned to attend that service algo. (applause.) He felt bound to say a word as a Nonconformist. He appreciated very filly indeed the unfailing courtesy whißh the Rector of Warrington had always shown to him and the manner in which he had dealt with what might have been a little difficulty. The attendance at his own church, which as a conscien- tious Nonconformist he felt Nund to give preference to and the strong desire that no src'ion of the community sh,,uld feel that he was desirous of even anneari,,g to offer a slight to them, had been met by the courteous sugtressian of the Rector that he (the Mayor) should attend the service at the Parish Church in the evening. Enhei all the friemis who were good enough to honour him with their company in the morning wohld maire a special point of accompanying him in the evening to the Pariph Church. (applause.)</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-11-17_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>BUSINESS TRANSACTED</head>
        <p>BUSINESS TRANSACTED</p>
        <p>The Council afterwards very speedily confirmed the appointment of the various committees for the engnine: year. The returning aldermen for the nine wards were re-elected.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-11-17_WidnesExaminer_art0029" n="art0029">
        <head>STOP A COUGH IN ONE NIGHT.</head>
        <p>STOP A COUGH IN ONE NIGHT.</p>
        <p>Take VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE. It stops an ordinary cough in one ni,ht, and cures chronic coughs, bronchitis, asthma, c3tsrr4h, influ,nzt, arid whooping cough rapidly. Its vast suporiority over the different emulsions and ordinary cough mix,nr,.4 cannot 13. mated. It has savad thousands of liveS after they hay, hen turned out of hospitals. r; is a new rici,,ntifiC remedy endmised by medicsl men. Ask for VENT° s LIGHTNING COUGH CURE, end see that you get it, price Is. and 2s. 91. per bottle (eopyrieht). sold by fol- lowing chemise KNOWLEs. Warrington ; Wtr.LBHIDGE, St. fielon4 ; PEARE. Esrlestown and Nawton ; FooGirr, Widnes ; WESTON, Runcorn ; and all chemists.</p>
