        <p>THE BEN EFITS OF SCIENCE. It is seldom that any discevery of s3ience is such as will beraifit all (lasso; of people. S)ant of the greatest discoveries of the ace, white they have proved directly henificial to thOUSathtia, have liso, at least for a time, injured other thou:ands. Even some of the bect medicinal precaratioas, however much they may do to remove ono cla:.s f dis.‘,se. or suit some constitutions, at the same time tither deepen the hold of another dis- ease, or leave it entirely untouched, or if they benefit one class of patient!-, they may injure another. Now the great need of the ago is some scientifically arranged pre— paration which will cope effectually with the prevalent diseases of this coantry,wt ich wiil be certain t) do good when fairly tried, which will he equally adapted to the needs of the merchant and tiv wrkman,the professional man, and he who wins his bread by the sweat of his brow, toe ,tudent, the clrrk,the factory htnd,the miner, and the roadside latourer. It should be. too, such a preparation as contaius no injurious ingr4dients, and which may be taken with impunity by the weakly child, or the delicate lady, as well as by the stronger constituted man. Such a discovery would devrve to be calf ad The Perfection of Medicinal Preparations, and would indeed be an Invaluable boon to Suffering Humanity. Now this much needed boon has been found, has been tried, and wherever proved, it has been found satisfactory. We refer to Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, th, Vege.table Tonic, which when once tried has be, n always recommended, and has proved success- ful when all other medicine has failed to give relief, and we may say further, that it has proved permawntly beneficial, when other preparations at best only give temporary relinf. It is strongly recommended as The Best Remedy of the Age for Indigestion in its different forms, such as Sick Headache, Pains in the Side, Giddi- ness,Lces of Appetite, a:so for Nervousness and Nervous Disorders. Sleeplessness, Neuralgia, Low Spirits, and all kinds or Wea'aness. It has often proved very beneficial to persons sufferim: from great Weakness, either after an illness, long confinement to ill-ventilated rooms, or any ether cau.e. It strikes at the source of the Disease, removing the cause of the illness, and strengthens those parts of the system which have been weakened by it, and therefore most liable to colds and other ailments. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters being purely vegetable, it is a Natural Tunin,and cuited to all ages at all seasons of the year. It is everywhere acknowledged to be a powerful aid in restoring the body to a healthy state when drranged by divase. If you suspect that your health is beginning to fail, brace up your nerves, and fortify your ctn. titution by taking nos, a course of this excellent Tonic, which is sold everywhere in battles at 23 91 and 4,i 61 each, but should any difficulty be ex- perienced in pr, curine it, the Proprietors will forward same for the ale we prices, carriage free. Avoid Imita- tions. When purchasing.,3er the name,"Gwilym Evans," on Label, Stamp, and Bottle. Sole Proprietors; Quinine Bitters Manufacturing, Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales.</p>
