        <p>At 11-ough an. The visitors star:AA against the wind, but the Ringers pressed anti nearly got through, Hallam saving splendidly. Warrington lost the services of Moores early on. From a scrimmage near the goal Sam Jamea nearly gut through, and sitortlY after the same player kicked a goal frt-tra a locality. : B oughton Rangers (A), one god ; WarrioWou A, nil. On mauling, Warrington played better and attacked strongly, and from a fret, kick tried a kick at goal.which wen n wide. The game was now kept to the triiddle of the fi)lcl for some time, Warrington having slightly the bettvr of the game. Warriugt-in then attacked strongly, but Broughton brae away and nearly scorcd. Warring- ton then attacked but could no score. Final : Broughton Rangers (A), one got; Warrington (A), nil.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE JUNIOR LEAGUE. Latchford Rangers v. Runcorn Hornets.</p>
