        <p>WITH a prudent use. has saved Jnany a life, and yet we think the idea might be improved upon and reduced to a more simple f0r.,,. 'rake some good Compound such a: COCKL".6'S ANTIBILIOUS PILLS, and we find that the desired end may be obtained without scales and weights, or little mysterious compartments, and enchanted bottles with crystal stoppers. Others might be used, but COCKLE'S PILLS, as tested by many thousands of persons, and found to answer their purposs so well, may be set down as the best.—Observer.</p>
